  "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 20-layer HfO2/SiO2 chirped dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (alternating, 10 pairs, starting with HfO2). Optimize all 20 layer thicknesses using gradient-based optimizer with smoothness regularization penalty (lambda = 0.1) applied to adjacent thickness differences. Initialize thickness bounds: odd-indexed layers (HfO2) 45-90 nm, even-indexed layers (SiO2) 65-130 nm, with ±10% chirp envelope around linear progression. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized or both TE/TM. Spectral bands: 400-700 nm (maximize reflectance), 1530-1565 nm (maximize transmittance). Total layer count fixed at 20. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design and optimize a 20-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 chirped dielectric stack on fused silica under normal unpolarized incidence to maximize reflectance in 400–700 nm and transmittance in 1530–1565 nm, while suppressing reverse-band leakage, using gradient-based thickness search with ±10% chirp bounds.",
